 "input": "ietf, roughly: someone posts an Internet-Draft to the datatracker. drafts expire after 6 months unless updated. if a working group adopts it, wg chairs run the adoption call on the mailing list, then working group last call later. after that it goes to the area director who reviews and asks for IETF last call (whole community, on the main list). then the IESG ballots on it, ADs can DISCUSS (block) until issues are fixed. approved docs go to the RFC Editor queue, they copy-edit, authors do AUTH48 final check, then it's published with a number. the datatracker shows state through all of this.",
 "expect_status": "ok",
